## Why We Win

**1. Self-hosted — code never leaves your machine**
Every direct competitor with real provenance capability is cloud SaaS: Span ($24/dev/month, cloud-only), Tabnine provenance ($39/user/month Enterprise, cloud-only), GitClear (SaaS). LineageLens stores everything in your own PostgreSQL instance. This is the deciding factor for regulated industries, government contractors, and any team with data residency or air-gap requirements.

**2. Real-time network-layer capture, not retroactive inference**
Span uses an ML classifier to infer AI origin after the fact (their stated 95% accuracy means 5% wrong, with no prompt data ever captured). GitClear depends on vendor telemetry APIs requiring each tool to expose its own data. LineageLens intercepts at the network layer — it sees the actual prompt and model response the moment it happens, for every AI tool, regardless of whether that vendor has an API for it.

**3. Tool-agnostic by architecture**
One proxy captures Claude Code, Cursor, Aider, Copilot, Codeium, Continue, and any tool that sends HTTP to an AI provider. Tabnine's provenance feature only covers Tabnine. GitClear needs each vendor to participate. LineageLens captures everything without asking vendors for anything.

**4. Risk scoring inside GitHub PRs before merge**
No competitor scores risk per insertion. LineageLens maps each insertion to a 0.0–1.0 risk score based on code pattern, model, and file context, surfaced as a GitHub PR comment before the code merges. Security teams can act before AI-generated code ships.

**5. Queryable from inside the AI chat via MCP**
The MCP server makes provenance queryable from Claude Code, Cursor, and Continue without leaving the conversation. Ask "what AI wrote this function and what was the prompt?" from inside the tool that wrote it. No competitor in this category has an MCP server.

**6. Compliance report without a $25K implementation fee**
Cycode and Secure Code Warrior charge enterprise implementation fees starting at $25,000 for AI governance reports. LineageLens ships a CEO and compliance-ready AI Usage Report at the Plus tier, self-hosted, at a fraction of that cost.

