## Why Now

AI coding adoption is already in production across engineering teams. Governance has not caught up. Three signals point to urgency:

1. **Cursor published Agent Trace** (February 2026) — an open RFC for AI code attribution. Platform players are moving to define the standard. Early adopters who already have provenance data will have a compliance head start.

2. **OWASP launched its AIBOM initiative** — the AI equivalent of a software bill of materials. Regulatory guidance on AI code supply chains is forming now, not later.

3. **Incidents are already happening** — AI-generated security vulnerabilities, hallucinated API usage, and auth logic written without full context are documented failure modes. The teams that instrument before the incident reconstruct; the teams that don't, guess.

The question is not whether teams will need to prove AI code origin. It is whether they build that audit trail proactively or reactively after an audit, a breach, or a regulator asks.
